  "claim": "R. M. Hare's is editor-in-chief of the journal which often features the ecological disarray of the writer of the ecopsychology book \"The Spell of the Sensuous: Perception and Language in a More-than-Human World.\" It is located in Denton, Texas.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Center for Environmental Philosophy. Sentence: The Center for Environmental Philosophy is located at the University of North Texas in Denton, Texas.\nPage: Environmental Ethics (journal). Sentence: The editor-in-chief is Eugene Hargrove and it is published by the Center for Environmental Philosophy (University of North Texas).\nPage: David Abram. Sentence: Abram is founder and creative director of the \"Alliance for Wild Ethics (AWE)\"; his essays on the cultural causes and consequences of ecological disarray have appeared often in such journals as \"Orion, Environmental Ethics, Parabola, Tikkun,\" and \"The Ecologist,\" as well as numerous anthologies.\nPage: Ecopsychology. Sentence: Two other books were especially formative for the field, Paul Shepard's 1982 volume, \"Nature and Madness,\" which explored the effect that our ever-diminishing engagement with wild nature had upon human psychological development, and philosopher David Abram's \"The Spell of the Sensuous: Perception and Language in a More-than-Human World,\" published in 1996.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Center for Environmental Philosophy. Sentence: The Center for Environmental Philosophy is located at the University of North Texas in Denton, Texas.\nPage: Environmental Ethics (journal). Sentence: The editor-in-chief is Eugene Hargrove and it is published by the Center for Environmental Philosophy (University of North Texas).\nPage: David Abram. Sentence: Abram is founder and creative director of the \"Alliance for Wild Ethics (AWE)\"; his essays on the cultural causes and consequences of ecological disarray have appeared often in such journals as \"Orion, Environmental Ethics, Parabola, Tikkun,\" and \"The Ecologist,\" as well as numerous anthologies.\nPage: Ecopsychology. Sentence: Two other books were especially formative for the field, Paul Shepard's 1982 volume, \"Nature and Madness,\" which explored the effect that our ever-diminishing engagement with wild nature had upon human psychological development, and philosopher David Abram's \"The Spell of the Sensuous: Perception and Language in a More-than-Human World,\" published in 1996.",
