        "original_id": "2b7d6ce7-42cf-5625-a54f-6787a0fb4da5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Center for Environmental Philosophy, Alliance for Wild Ethics\n- Places: University of North Texas, Denton, Texas\n- People: Eugene Hargrove, David Abram, Paul Shepard\n- Products: Environmental Ethics, Nature and Madness, The Spell of the Sensuous: Perception and Language in a More-than-Human World\n- Topics: Ecopsychology\n\nFacts:\n- The Center for Environmental Philosophy is located at the University of North Texas in Denton, Texas.\n- In 1982, Paul Shepard published Nature and Madness, a book described as especially formative for ecopsychology.\n- In 1996, David Abram published The Spell of the Sensuous: Perception and Language in a More-than-Human World, a book described as especially formative for ecopsychology.\n- David Abram is the founder and creative director of the Alliance for Wild Ethics.\n- David Abram's essays on ecological disarray have appeared in journals including Environmental Ethics.\n- Environmental Ethics is published by the Center for Environmental Philosophy at the University of North Texas.\n- Eugene Hargrove is the editor-in-chief of Environmental Ethics.",
